<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Studio-generated helpdesk.ticket view records, ported from
    Clear-DB (Jinasena production) into Fix-repair's on-disk XML.

    Background
    ==========
    During the earlier Studio→Python migration, four
    "Odoo Studio: helpdesk.ticket.*" ir.ui.view records had their
    ir.model.data xmlid ownership REPINNED from studio_customization
    to Fix-repair — but the actual arch_db content stayed in the
    Clear-DB records only, never landing in any on-disk XML file.

    Result: on the production DB the views work (records exist from
    Studio's original create); on any fresh install of Fix-repair
    the views are never re-created and the helpdesk.ticket form
    reverts to the base + Python-only inherits, losing every
    Studio-added field placement, tab, and grouping.

    This file re-materialises the arch on disk. Each <record> reuses
    the exact xmlid Fix-repair.ir.model.data already has for the
    view, so on Clear-DB upgrade the existing DB record is updated
    in-place (same arch → no functional change); on stand-alone
    install the record is created fresh with the correct arch.

    Idempotent by definition — arch_db reflects exactly what
    Clear-DB currently serves.

    All 91 x_studio_* field references in these arches are already
    Python-declared in Fix-repair (audited 2026-08-12). No extra
    field declarations needed.
-->
<odoo>

    <record id="view_helpdesk_ticket_form_4012" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">Odoo Studio: helpdesk.ticket.form customization</field>
        <field name="model">helpdesk.ticket</field>
